{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via an automated cobbler/orchestrator pipeline) requested implementation of srd064 R2.1-R2.4 for the `cmd/shuf` utility. This is task #5425 in generation run 44. The specific requirements are:\n   - R2.1: `-i LO-HI` / `--input-range=LO-HI` — generate and shuffle integers from LO to HI inclusive\n   - R2.2: `-n COUNT` / `--head-count=COUNT` — output at most COUNT lines\n   - R2.3: `-r` / `--repeat` — sampling with replacement; without -n, runs indefinitely\n   - R2.4: `-o FILE` / `--output=FILE` — write output to FILE instead of stdout\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/shuf/main.go` and `cmd/shuf/shuf_test.go`. Must preserve existing R1.1-R1.4 functionality.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go unix utility reimplementation with differential testing against GNU reference binary (`gshuf`)\n   - Non-deterministic output requires structural property verification (line count, value ranges, uniqueness) not exact byte comparison\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` and `testutils.BuildBinary` for differential testing\n   - `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` required at start of main\n   - SPDX copyright header required on all Go files\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max (E8)\n   - File size limit: 500 lines max (E9)\n   - No git commands allowed (orchestrator manages git)\n   - `go build -o bin/shuf ./cmd/shuf/` for compilation\n   - Tests with `go test ./cmd/shuf/... -count=1`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd064-shuf.yaml`\n     - Full SRD with requirements R1-R4, non-goals, and acceptance criteria\n     - R2.1: `-i LO-HI` integer range generation, must not combine with file args\n     - R2.2: `-n COUNT` head count limiting\n     - R2.3: `-r` repeat mode, indefinite without -n\n     - R2.4: `-o FILE` output file redirection\n     - Non-goals: no specific PRNG algorithm, no --random-source compatibility testing\n\n   - `cmd/shuf/main.go` (existing, needs modification)\n     - Very basic implementation: no flag parsing, all args treated as filenames\n     - Uses `math/rand/v2`, `bufio`, `fmt`, `os`, `pkg/sys`\n     - `main()`: reads lines, shuffles with rand.Shuffle, writes to stdout\n     - `readLines(args)`: defaults to stdin if no args, iterates file args\n     - `readFileLines(name)`: opens file or uses stdin for \"-\", uses bufio.Scanner\n     ```go\n     package main\n     import (\n         \"bufio\"\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"math/rand/v2\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         lines, err := readLines(os.Args[1:])\n         if err != nil {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"shuf: %v\\n\", err)\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n         rand.Shuffle(len(lines), func(i, j int) {\n             lines[i], lines[j] = lines[j], lines[i]\n         })\n         w := bufio.NewWriter(os.Stdout)\n         for _, line := range lines {\n             fmt.Fprintln(w, line)\n         }\n         if err := w.Flush(); err != nil {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"shuf: write error: %v\\n\", err)\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n     }\n     func readLines(args []string) ([]string, error) { /* reads from files or stdin */ }\n     func readFileLines(name string) ([]string, error) { /* opens single file or stdin */ }\n     ```\n\n   - `cmd/shuf/shuf_test.go` (existing, needs modification)\n     - Has `sortLines` normalizer for differential tests\n     - `TestDiff`: empty input, single line, multiple lines, no trailing newline (with sortLines normalizer)\n     - `TestDiffFile`: file argument test\n     - `TestMultipleFiles`: structural test verifying permutation of combined file contents\n     - `TestDiffStdinDash`: stdin via \"-\" argument\n     - `TestPermutation`: structural verification that output is a permutation\n     - `TestNoTrailingNewline`: last line without newline is included\n     - All use `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` and `exec.LookPath(\"gshuf\")` with skip\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet — implementation has not begun.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read all three required files (SRD, existing main.go, existing test file)\n   - Analyzed the gap: existing code has zero flag parsing, needs complete flag handling for -i, -n, -r, -o\n   - The main challenge is that the existing code passes all args as filenames; need to add proper flag parsing while preserving existing behavior\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The full task description with role, repository_files, project_context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, requirement_states), execution_constitution, go_style_constitution, task details, shared_protocols, and package_contracts. This is the automated stitch task prompt.\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — requesting this summary.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Implement flag parsing in `cmd/shuf/main.go` for `-i LO-HI`, `-n COUNT`, `-r`, `-o FILE`\n   - Implement `-i` range mode: generate integers LO to HI, validate format, error if combined with file args\n   - Implement `-n` head count: limit output to at most COUNT lines\n   - Implement `-r` repeat mode: sampling with replacement, indefinite without -n\n   - Implement `-o` output file: write to file instead of stdout\n   - Add differential tests and structural tests for all R2.1-R2.4 scenarios\n   - Verify: `go build -o bin/shuf ./cmd/shuf/`, `go test ./cmd/shuf/... -count=1`, `go vet ./cmd/shuf/...`\n   - Ensure existing R1.1-R1.4 tests still pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all three input files (SRD, main.go, test file) and was about to begin implementation. No